{#
  A photograph, untouched, with a sparse abstract panel joined beneath it.

  The arrangement comes from the photo-abstract-editorial Codex skill
  (github.com/ZzzLc0405/photo-abstract-editorial). That skill is offered for
  personal and non-commercial use only, so none of its text is reproduced
  here — what is adapted is the composition: the photo kept whole rather than
  filtered, a quiet panel of marks below it, one restrained serif title, and
  ivory everywhere else.

  One thing does not survive the translation, and it matters when describing
  the page to an owner. In the original the marks are read out of the
  photograph. A template renders before anyone has looked at the image, so
  these marks are built from the palette instead. They are a composition, not
  a reading of their photo — do not claim otherwise in the pitch.

  The photo is contained rather than cropped, so a wide image letterboxes into
  the ivory. That is the intended behaviour: this direction preserves the
  frame it was given.
#}
{% extends "_base.html.j2" %}
{% block style %}
{# Oyster, not ivory. The original skill calls for ivory and I set #f4f0e8,
   which lands three points from #F4F1EA — the exact warm cream the
   frontend-design skill names as the AI default. Shifting the ground neutral
   keeps the letterboxing reading as a gallery mat rather than as the tint
   every generated page arrives in. #}
body{background:#e7e6e1}
.hero{margin:0}
{# 62vh, not more: past that the business name falls below the fold on a
   laptop, and a demo whose first screen omits the name is a bad demo however
   good the photograph is. #}
.plate{width:100%;max-height:62vh;object-fit:contain;background:#dcdbd5}
.panel{padding:3.5rem 1.5rem}
.panel-inner{max-width:46rem;margin:0 auto}
{# Capped, so the marks keep the same weight on a wide screen as on a phone.
   Left to span 46rem they stretch into hairlines and read as a rendering
   fault rather than a composition. #}
.marks{display:block;width:100%;max-width:30rem;height:auto;margin-bottom:2.75rem}
.eyebrow{font-size:.68rem;letter-spacing:.24em;text-transform:uppercase;
  opacity:.45;margin:0 0 1rem}
h1{font-family:'Iowan Old Style',Palatino,'Palatino Linotype',Georgia,serif;
  font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(2.4rem,7.5vw,4.2rem);line-height:1.05;
  letter-spacing:-.015em;margin:0}
.lede{max-width:32rem;margin-top:1.6rem;font-size:1rem;opacity:.72}
.credit{padding:0 1.5rem;text-align:right}
h2{font-family:'Iowan Old Style',Palatino,Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;
  font-size:.72rem;letter-spacing:.22em;text-transform:uppercase;
  opacity:.5;margin:0 0 1.6rem}
h3{font-family:'Iowan Old Style',Palatino,Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;
  font-size:1.2rem;margin:2rem 0 .6rem}
.band{padding:4.5rem 0;border-top:1px solid rgba(60,55,45,.14)}
.item{border:0}
.item .dots{opacity:.22}
.facts-grid{display:grid;gap:3rem}
@media(min-width:820px){.facts-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}}
.gallery{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:2.5rem}
@media(min-width:820px){.gallery{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}}
.closing{background:rgba(60,55,45,.05)}
{% endblock %}

{% block hero %}
<header class="hero">
  {% if images %}<img class="plate" src="{{ images[0] }}" alt="">{% endif %}
  <div class="panel">
    <div class="panel-inner">
      {#
        Five marks, no more: an axis, a mass, a rhythm, a subject, an
        interval. Adding a sixth is what turns this from a panel into
        decoration.
      #}
      <svg class="marks" viewBox="0 0 600 180" role="presentation" aria-hidden="true">
        <rect x="0" y="96" width="228" height="52" fill="{{ palette.accent }}" opacity=".16"/>
        <line x1="0" y1="96" x2="600" y2="96" stroke="{{ palette.ink }}"
          stroke-width="1" opacity=".38"/>
        <circle cx="438" cy="62" r="46" fill="none" stroke="{{ palette.ink }}"
          stroke-width="1" opacity=".45"/>
        <line x1="292" y1="30" x2="292" y2="96" stroke="{{ palette.ink }}"
          stroke-width="1" opacity=".28"/>
        <line x1="324" y1="52" x2="324" y2="96" stroke="{{ palette.ink }}"
          stroke-width="1" opacity=".28"/>
        <line x1="340" y1="74" x2="340" y2="96" stroke="{{ palette.ink }}"
          stroke-width="1" opacity=".28"/>
        <line x1="0" y1="148" x2="228" y2="148" stroke="{{ palette.accent }}"
          stroke-width="2"/>
      </svg>
      {% if address or phone %}
      <p class="eyebrow">{{ address or phone }}</p>
      {% endif %}
      <h1>{{ business }}</h1>
      {% if about %}<p class="lede">{{ about }}</p>{% endif %}
    </div>
  </div>
  {% if stock_used %}<p class="credit">{{ stock_note }}</p>{% endif %}
</header>
{% endblock %}
